page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The pedagogical ladder · Ada Research</title><style>__CSS__</style></head><body><main><nav><a href="ca-elementary-rules.html#in-museum">← Inside the current hall</a><a href="/museum-progress?sequence=cellularautomata">Museum progress</a><a href="fractal-learning-arc.html">Fractals → L-systems</a><a href="learning-ladder.md">Full proposal</a></nav><div class="eyebrow">Possible bodies / the pedagogical ladder</div><h1>What can the next body do?</h1><p class="lead">Every hall gives us another capability—and another assumption we can press. The thread is what we can now predict, make or question with the tools we have acquired.</p><p class="notice">Proposal for discussion · 13 September 2026. Current maps, artifacts and route are preserved. The CA order below is a recommendation; its omitted comparison hall and missing live experiments need preparation.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Bring a capability</span><span class="chip">Predict and try</span><span class="chip">Follow the actual code</span><span class="chip">Press an assumption</span><span class="chip">Carry it elsewhere</span></div><section><h2>A ladder with returns</h2><p>Random walks already have state. Forces already couple bodies. Cellular automata adds a particular way of organising local updates across stored sites. The new chapter lets those earlier discoveries meet a neighbourhood rule.</p><p>A familiar operation can return as a wall, a path, an outfit or another agent. The new material lets us ask what the operation now permits, and what it still cannot express.</p></section><section><div class="tabs"><button data-seq="ca" aria-pressed="true">Cellular automata · proposed</button><button data-seq="randomness" aria-pressed="false">Randomness · current order</button><button data-seq="noise" aria-pressed="false">Noise · current order</button></div><div class="ladder"><div id="steps" class="steps" aria-label="Choose a rung"></div><article id="detail" class="detail" aria-live="polite"></article></div></section><section><h2>The proposed CA thread</h2><p class="route">row → recorded past → plane → volume + lingering state → visitor feedback → richer coupling → perturbation → recursive comparison</p><p>The Rule 30 bridge and the Life dish come before the three-dimensional builder so those differences can be discovered separately. The builder remains. The two-work comparison currently called Agents and Circuits becomes the proposed hinge into fractals.</p><p>The first transfer is now built: <a href="ca-history-bridge.html">one history, three museum bodies</a>. The next transfer is also built: <a href="ca-life-addresses.html">Life cells drive three room lamps</a>. <a href="ca-proximity.html">The visitor now enters the surface update</a>, with graded health and physical support. <a href="ca-soft-rules.html">CA_SoftRules now adds matched reaction–diffusion and curved wall coatings</a>. <a href="ca-edge-difference.html">CA_EdgeOfChaos now follows one difference through matched volumes, storage and architectural displays</a>. Next active hall: Fractal_Recursion.</p></section><details><summary>Read the full ladder, evidence and next actions</summary><div class="reading">__BODY__</div></details><footer><p><a href="learning-ladder.json">Structured plan</a> · <a href="learning-ladder.md">Markdown proposal</a></p><p>Future halls should earn their claims through observations and code. One central question does not impose a one-artifact limit.</p></footer></main><script>__SCRIPT__</script></body></html>'''
script='''const plan=__DATA__;let sequence='ca',selected=0;const el=id=>document.getElementById(id);function paragraph(label,text){const h=document.createElement('div');h.className='label';h.textContent=label;const p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent=text;el('detail').append(h,p);}function draw(){const list=el('steps');list.replaceChildren();plan[sequence].forEach((r,i)=>{const b=document.createElement('button');b.textContent=(i+1)+'. '+r.title;b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',i===selected?'true':'false');b.onclick=()=>{selected=i;draw();};list.append(b);});const r=plan[sequence][selected],detail=el('detail');detail.replaceChildren();const small=document.createElement('div');small.className='small';small.textContent=r.map+(sequence==='ca'?(r.active?' · in the current museum':' · currently outside the active route'):'');const title=document.createElement('h2');title.textContent=r.title;detail.append(small,title);for(const [key,label]of [['inherit','Bring'],['addition','New capability'],['encounter','Existing material'],['experiment','Discover'],['crack','Press the assumption'],['transfer','Carry forward'],['readiness','Readiness'],['next_action','Next actionable improvement']])if(r[key])paragraph(label,r[key]);const link=document.createElement('a');link.href='/necklace/thread?map='+encodeURIComponent(r.map)+'&role=primary';link.textContent='See the room’s current primary artifacts';detail.append(link);}document.querySelectorAll('[data-seq]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{sequence=b.dataset.seq;selected=0;document.querySelectorAll('[data-seq]').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',x===b?'true':'false'));draw();});draw();'''.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False).replace('</','<\\/'))
save(O/'learning-ladder.html',page.replace('__CSS__',css).replace('__BODY__',markdown.markdown(document,extensions=['tables','fenced_code'])).replace('__SCRIPT__',script))
manifest=['possible-bodies/learning-ladder.'+ext for ext in ['html','md','json']]
save(REC/'publish-targets.json',json.dumps(manifest,indent=2));save(REC/'publish-hashes.json',json.dumps({p:hashlib.sha256((R/'doc/research'/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()for p in manifest},indent=2))
save(REC/'README.md','''# Pedagogical ladder proposal — 13 September 2026

Palle asked for a good pedagogical ladder in CA and the adjacent/earlier sequences. The proposal uses actual active routes, primary roles, final texts and source inspection. It proposes a row/history/plane/volume progression, identifies the Soft Rules live-experiment gap, and positions the omitted CA_AgentsCircuits comparison as a possible hinge to fractals. The existing museum order, placements, roles and book texts are unchanged.

Deliverables: doc/research/possible-bodies/learning-ladder.md, learning-ladder.json and learning-ladder.html. Rebuild with tools/build_learning_ladder.py. The structured proposal records source paths, readiness and one concrete next improvement per CA room. The randomness/noise tables retain their current active order; later links are proposed transfer questions, not new runtime acceptance.

Current transfer: CA_GameOfLife has a shared history desk, support tiles and ornamental lattice, with desktop evidence and a revised final at ca-history-bridge.html. CA_BeyondBinary now adds a Life dish, fixed-address witnesses and three explicitly connected lamps, with 30 desktop checks and a revised passage at ca-life-addresses.html. CA_ExpandingSpace now has a proximity witness, real support/recovery, matched schedules and a shared wall frieze, with 36 desktop checks at ca-proximity.html. CA_SoftRules now has matched live fields, shared table/wall textures and two primary passages, with 37 desktop checks at ca-soft-rules.html. CA_EdgeOfChaos now has 45 desktop checks for matched 3D runs, independent coefficients, storage, slices, controls and walking. All five works remain; next active hall is Fractal_Recursion. Consider the route changes only with coherent adjacent book passages and navigation. Preserve existing confident works; one primary was a scaffold, not a limit.
''')
print('Built the proposal: 8 CA rungs, 7 randomness rungs, 8 noise rungs. No live route or artifact edits.')

